From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 06:05:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(render): marshal off-context native calls onto the
 context thread

Kotlin can call into native from a non-context thread (coroutines on
background dispatchers, K/N workers). Async calls are now re-posted to the
context thread on Android, iOS and OHOS; sync calls made off-context fail
loudly instead of mutating render state from the wrong thread. The sync
method classification is shared per platform. On iOS, FireFatalException
from a worker hops synchronously onto the #1566 context thread so crash
reporting no longer trips the context-thread assertion.

Fork-Patch: render-marshal-offcontext-native-calls
Origin: af2c4d51 25cbc1fa 9ba11795
Upstream-Status: pending
Signed-off-by: BiSheng <raft-mobile-bisheng@mail.build>
